Linus,

please pull sound fixes for v2.6.39-rc1 from:

  git://git.kernel.org/pub/scm/linux/kernel/git/tiwai/sound-2.6.git for-linus

This contains the last-minute fixes picked up recently, including
two OSS security fixes, a couple of long-standing regression fixes,
asihpi minor updates, and a few quirks for USB-audio and HD-audio.


Thanks!

Takashi

===

Benjamin Herrenschmidt (1):
      ALSA: vmalloc buffers should use normal mmap

Clemens Ladisch (1):
      ALSA: usb-audio: add Cakewalk UM-1G support

Dan Rosenberg (2):
      sound/oss: remove offset from load_patch callbacks
      sound/oss/opl3: validate voice and channel indexes

David Henningsson (1):
      ALSA: HDA: New AD1984A model for Dell Precision R5500

Eliot Blennerhassett (3):
      ALSA: asihpi - Support single-rate no-SRC cards
      ALSA: asihpi - Improve non-busmaster adapter operation
      ALSA: asihpi - Update verbose debug print macros

Keith A. Milner (1):
      ALSA: usb-audio - Support for Boss JS-8 Jam Station

Takashi Iwai (2):
      ALSA: hda - Fix SPDIF out regression on ALC889
      ALSA: Fix yet another race in disconnection

